A||N||1||bilbo||Dying seat covers question???||||1||
Z||000000||bilbo||05-14-2001||05:51 PM||||Has anyone ever dyed original seat covers? I just got a set of perfect 84 seats with the speakers in the headrests but they're tan.I was wondering if I removed seat upholstry if I could dye it black or something,anyone????!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||05-14-2001||06:27 PM||||I've gone from silver/grey to tan on some Grand-Am seats I had in a pickup truck. It worked very well ecxept that the dye doesn't change the color of the vynil piping very well. I dismantled the seats and removed the covers, then used like three boxes of RIT fabric dye (available at K-Mart or any fabric outlet) in a big wash tub sink. Follow the directions on the box. I was very pleased with mine, they still looked great after five years when I sold the truck. ||||reg||14
